implement: root cause confirmed — substituteIdentifiers did raw replacement, and the a-r template embeds <reason> inside a single-quoted --summary segment, so an apostrophe terminated the quote early (bash: unexpected EOF ... matching quote).

Approach (scoped to packages/herdr/src/form-dialog.ts): shell-escape substituted values for shell-route templates (\!/\!\! prefix) only. A minimal context scanner determines whether each placeholder sits inside an existing single-quoted, double-quoted, or unquoted segment, and escapes accordingly:
- single-quoted context (a-r <reason>, <producer_comment>): close/escape/reopen apostrophes (`'\''`) — no re-wrapping (re-wrapping would unbalance the template quotes);
- double-quoted context: escape \, ", $, backtick;
- unquoted context (<title>, <status>, <stage>, <search_term>, <author>): full POSIX single-quote wrap.

Agent-prompt templates (/skill:*, /intake, /plan, /prompt:, /herdr:note-edit) keep raw substitution — their values are argv elements, never shell-parsed. No template changes needed, so chord bindings/visible behaviour are unchanged. Tests: form-dialog.test.ts now includes context-specific escaping cases plus bash round-trip regressions (apostrophes, full metacharacter set, newlines, double-quote context, injection) that execute the generated command and assert verbatim output. Full herdr suite green (2720 tests).

